  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Sample selection models for count data in R (2017) in Computational Statistics. 9 citations.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Sample selection models for count data in R (2017) in Computational Statistics is authored by Karol Wyszynski and Giampiero Marra. Topics: Covariate, Selection (genetic algorithm), Model selection, R package and Computer science.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">9 citations (OpenAlex). Citations peaked in 2018 with 2 citing works. Citing venues include The International Journal of Health Planning and Management, Computational Statistics & Data Analysis and Statistical Methods in Medical Research.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Limited online visibility beyond citations.</p>",
